.DS_Store
node_modules/
.impeccable/

# Claude Code project config IS shared/versioned (CLAUDE.md, .claude/settings.json, hooks/,
# skills/) -- (/stress-test finding, independent reviewer, 2026-09-03): a blanket `.claude/` line
# here since before this session started (2026-09-03) silently ignored EVERY file added today
# (settings.json, the pre-push hook, the project-scoped stress-test skill) with zero prior
# investigation of why -- defeating their whole stated purpose ("closes that hole for any push
# made from inside a Claude Code session") for anyone but this one local machine. Only the genuine
# per-user local override file is excluded, the standard Claude Code convention (same pattern
# ruflo-runtime's own .gitignore already uses for its 2 machine-generated .claude/ files).
.claude/settings.local.json
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Internal session research — comp anchors, gate scores, blocklists. Local only,
# never published to the public repo.
otak-session-notes.md
pipeline/output/
pipeline/.venv/
.private/

# Any local Python virtualenv, wherever it's created (/stress-test finding, 2026-09-02):
# .venv_stress_verify/ (58MB, DuckDB stdlib bindings) was relying SOLELY on its own
# auto-generated internal .gitignore (a `*` rule every `python -m venv` writes) to stay out of
# this PUBLIC repo's history -- nothing at the repo-root level actually covered it. That's fragile:
# any venv tool that doesn't self-ignore, or a `git add -f`, would land 58MB of binaries in public
# git history. Covers this one explicitly, plus any future differently-named venv.
.venv_stress_verify/
.venv/
venv/
